      "summaries": {
        "en": "OpenClaw Windows Node is a companion suite that brings OpenClaw's clipboard management to Windows via a system tray app, shared library, Node.js bindings, and a PowerToys Command Palette extension. It enables seamless clipboard history, search, and sync across devices. The modular architecture allows developers to integrate clipboard functionality into their own tools or extend it with custom plugins. Try it to supercharge your clipboard workflow or build new utilities on top of its API.",
        "zh": "OpenClaw Windows Node是OpenClaw在Windows平台的伴侣套件，通过系统托盘应用、共享库、Node.js绑定和PowerToys命令面板扩展，实现强大的剪贴板管理。它解决跨设备同步、历史搜索和高效粘贴等痛点，模块化设计便于开发者集成或扩展。技术亮点在于共享库与Node绑定提供灵活API，使非.NET应用也能调用核心功能。用户可直接使用系统托盘应用体验无缝管理，或利用API构建自定义剪贴板增强工具。",
        "es": "OpenClaw Windows Node is a companion suite that brings OpenClaw's clipboard management to Windows via a system tray app, shared library, Node.js bindings, and a PowerToys Command Palette extension. It enables seamless clipboard history, search, and sync across devices. The modular architecture allows developers to integrate clipboard functionality into their own tools or extend it with custom plugins. Try it to supercharge your clipboard workflow or build new utilities on top of its API.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "openclaw-windows-node gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "OpenClaw Windows Node is a companion suite that brings OpenClaw's clipboard management to Windows via a system tray app, shared library, Node.js bindings, and a PowerToys Command Palette extension. It enables seamless clipboard history, search, and sync across devices. The modular architecture allows developers to integrate clipboard functionality into their own tools or extend it with custom plugins. Try it to supercharge your clipboard workflow or build new utilities on top of its API.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw-windows-node for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
